# Denoising a raw photograph.
#
# image() already inserted hot_pixel_repair and the demosaic, so `src` here is
# a finished RGB image and the noise left in it is the broad-band sensor kind.
#
# Denoise runs AFTER develop, and that ordering is measured rather than a
# preference. A shrinkage threshold is a fixed distance in the value domain, so
# ahead of a tone curve it thresholds in linear scene space where shadow detail
# is compressed into a tiny range. On an under-exposed ARW pushed 1.85 stops,
# denoising first kept 6% of the detail against 88% for denoising after.

src = image("test")

developed = params(basic_adjust, auto_exposure = 1)(src)

# The luma range is deliberately much smaller than chroma's.
#
# On a Bayer sensor green is sampled at half of all sites while red and blue
# get a quarter each, so the pixel-scale speckle -- the coloured dots visible
# when you zoom in -- is overwhelmingly CHROMA. Luma needs very little: the
# whole luma detail of a developed photo measures around 0.02, so a threshold
# anywhere near that erases the picture rather than the noise.
luma   = slider("luma", 0.0, 0.03, 0.005)
chroma = slider("chroma", 0.0, 0.25, 0.08)
levels = slider("levels", 1, 6, 4)

clean = wavelet_denoise(developed, luma = luma, chroma = chroma, levels = levels)

display(developed, "original")
display(clean,     "denoised")
